    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_51f75e0d16ecefacbeb8c403793eb46436969988551f21c13c9804ff8f250f9b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source constructs circular and hyperbolic logarithmic moments in parallel. On the circular side, a unit-circle contour produces log-sine moments and an arcsine series generates a K_m hierarchy; on the hyperbolic side, exponential factorization exposes log-sinh moments and the substitution x↦ix turns the arcsine identities into inverse-hyperbolic-sine identities used to build the analogous F_m hierarchy.",
