    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8f57b0f78d28364ba6196df025cad13d1b3336a3c1e1ea27450f9a6a3ba42c54",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across Sections 2 and 3, the source first exposes logarithmic moments by changing representation—factoring an exponential expression through 2 sinh(θ/2), or converting a unit-circle contour into real log-sine integrals—and then separates index parity through f(2m)+g(2m) versus f(2m-1)-g(2m-1), or through real versus imaginary parts. This shared architecture organizes parity-indexed families instead of evaluating isolated zeta values.",
